# Arc Ledger — <FILL-IN: arc name>

> **APPEND-ONLY.** This file is the arc's single running ledger. The
> discipline:
>
> 1. **Append at every decision, gate verdict, or halt.** Never rewrite,
>    reorder, or delete history — a corrected verdict gets a NEW entry
>    that supersedes the old one by date, with the old entry left intact.
> 2. **On resume, read the ledger TAIL first** so you do not re-dispatch
>    completed work. The tail is the arc's authoritative "where are we".
> 3. **One ledger per arc.** When an arc closes, open a fresh ledger for
>    the next arc and link the closed one from its opening entry; the
>    closing entry names the closure doc / checkpoint that carries the
>    arc's full record.
> 4. **Each entry carries:** date · what was decided/verified · the
>    verdict (PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/RULED) · pointers to the detail (doc path,
>    commit hash, test command).
>
> Why append-only: rewritten history is how drift enters — a "cleaned up"
> ledger silently erases the failed attempt the next session needed to
> know about. The ledger is evidence, not narrative.

